ere the geese  at crater is off the top of my head it's  a relatively small area located to the  west of the tip and the tower clearly  visible from the tower itself scouting  the area you can find several you know  craters that are smaller in size  surrounding a rather large one as if  this wasn't already obvious at this  point the fact that craters pepper the  ground in this area imply some sort of  series of massive impacts made by very  hard objects striking the surface of the  earth at immensely high velocities but  will expand on that in just a bit inside  most of the craters we can actually see  what made those gigantic impacts their  rocks as expected but not just any rocks  living rocks to be specific the smaller  craters have stone peb lights inside  them and the large crater has a straight  up stone talus housed right smack in the  dead center of the impact implying that  it was the once airborne flying object  that struck this piece of the earth and  created this crater now even though this  is the only area in the land of hyrule  that features these strange craters  there is still a heck of a lot of  information that we can read into and  facts that we can logically deduce from  what we've just seen in this game and  previous zelda games so let's talk about  it in the first place the idea of the  stone Tallis's being aliens isn't even  that crazy of a notion because aliens  existing in zelda games is really  nothing new at all the most iconic  appearance of aliens from outer space in  this franchise will probably come to  mind immediately for the more savvy of  you  their who have played the beloved  majora's mask in the game as a sidequest  helping out a little redheaded farm girl  named Romani of course not to be  confused for the alternate universe  equivalent redheaded farm girl named  Malin or even the other redheaded girl  named Maren and the Zelda developers  really liked this character anyway  Romani has a little side quest that  Lincoln helped 