ombat by guardians implying a  difference or lack of affiliation for  the Stoney's so given that one of these  rock giants is found right in the middle  of a giant crater in the middle of other  smaller craters the last question we  have to ask is how were these craters  made exactly are we 100% certain that  the only way the craters were created is  from these stone guys falling from orbit  first I tried to theorize about the  possibility that they were spewed out  from within Death Mountain and came to  life somehow but I don't think that  flying through the air from Death  Mountain peak would create a big enough  impact to cause this much damage to the  earth especially for the tiny little  stone pivots which created the smaller  craters  in my opinion the only way these large  craters formed here is from the big  stone talus &amp; Co falling from outer  space and crash landing on planet Hyrule  and since they're alive that can only  mean one thing  aliens so there you have it actually one  more thing I'll cover is since the  Stoney's are present all over Hyrule why  aren't their craters all over Hyrule if  the stone talus is truly came from outer  space how else would they have gotten  dispersed across the land well allow me  to direct the attention to one little  bitty concept that will nicely wrap this  theory up with a neat little bow on top  I mentioned earlier that pebble 'its  grow up to be stone Tallis's right as in  they're essentially babies right well  can't there be more babies made actually  there are some stone telus bosses that  seem to confirm this possibility look at  these two unique ones in particular one  is called stone talus senior and the  other is called stone talus junior  senior and junior the only thing this  implies is a parent and child familial  relation if it was simply referring to  size it would instead be major and minor  and if it was only referring to the age  of the monsters it would be something  like ancient and young but in